ext":"Start with an example… The Problem","targetRectangle":{"y":79,"x":99,"width":1448.4000012539325,"height":100.53440856933594}},{"text":"Suppose you need three counts from a list of marks: ","targetRectangle":{"y":212.85752868652344,"x":116.19349670410156,"width":809.03520000000049,"height":53.599999666213989}},{"text":"how many passed, ","targetRectangle":{"y":266.45752835273743,"x":148.59349817790485,"width":297.74520000000001,"height":53.599999666213989}},{"text":"how many failed, ","targetRectangle":{"y":320.05752801895142,"x":148.59349817790485,"width":268.57260000000002,"height":53.599999666213989}},{"text":"how many are firsts. ","targetRectangle":{"y":373.65752768516541,"x":148.59349817790485,"width":317.34180000000009,"height":53.599999666213989}},{"text":"The three loops are identical except for the test inside the if. ","targetRectangle":{"y":480.85752701759338,"x":116.19349670410156,"width":729.72540000000049,"height":94.599999666213989}},{"text":"The issue is the same loop is typed three times, and a mistake in it has to be found and fixed three times.","targetRectangle":{"y":575.45752668380737,"x":116.19349670410156,"width":802.7082000000006,"height":94.599999666213989}},{"text":"Nine lines of loop to produce three numbers. A fourth count would be three more lines.","targetRectangle":{"y":670.05752635002136,"x":148.59349817790485,"width":722.20140000000049,"height":94.599999666213989}},{"text":"The part that matters, the test, is one short expression buried in the middle of each loop.","targetRectangle":{"y":764.65752601623535,"x":148.59349817790485,"width":687.96720000000039,"height":94.599999666213989}},{"text":"Nothing links the three loops together. Change how one of them works and the other two stay as they were.","targetRectangle":{"y":859.25752568244934,"x":148.59349817790485,"width":765.15660000000048,"height":122.04240417480469}}],"baseLayer":{"animations":[],"initialState":{"affineTransform":[1,0,0,1,0,0],"masksToBounds":false,"rotation":